(7512134, 1199003, 188948, '<td valign="top">I like this picture, I like the color of the birds, and they all seem pretty sharp to me.  Good job!</td>', 'I like this picture, I like the color of the birds, and they all seem pretty sharp to me.  Good job!', '2017-05-06 11:56:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7512163, 1198910, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is fascinating to me - how did you do this?</td>', 'This is fascinating to me - how did you do this?', '2017-05-06 19:20:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7512216, 1198910, 35044, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> This is fascinating to me - how did you do this? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi, I trimmed half my beard, tidied half my face, and untidied the other. I draped a work shirt over one shoulder. I set up a single soft box, on one side.  <br/> <br/>My wife pressed the shutter, and I post processed by setting up two different white balances and tones, masking one half to get the two tone look.</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: This is fascinating to me - how did you do this?   Hi, I trimmed half my beard, tidied half my face, and untidied the other. I draped a work shirt over one shoulder. I set up a single soft box, on one side.   My wife pressed the shutter, and I post processed by setting up two different white balances and tones, masking one half to get the two tone look.', '2017-05-07 15:03:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7512390, 1198910, 30982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Matthew:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> This is fascinating to me - how did you do this? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi, I trimmed half my beard, tidied half my face, and untidied the other. I draped a work shirt over one shoulder. I set up a single soft box, on one side.  <br/> <br/>My wife pressed the shutter, and I post processed by setting up two different white balances and tones, masking one half to get the two tone look. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks!  I was wondering how you got the different tones.  Very clever!  I appreciate the explanation.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Matthew: Originally posted by Melethia: This is fascinating to me - how did you do this?   Hi, I trimmed half my beard, tidied half my face, and untidied the other. I draped a work shirt over one shoulder. I set up a single soft box, on one side.   My wife pressed the shutter, and I post processed by setting up two different white balances and tones, masking one half to get the two tone look.  Thanks!  I was wondering how you got the different tones.  Very clever!  I appreciate the explanation.', '2017-05-08 00:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
